== Preface

Dear friends, I heartily commend the following discourse on closet prayer to your#super[+] serious reading. I have many reasons to hope that when you#super[+] have once read it through, you#super[+] will be more in love with closet prayer than ever, that you#super[+] will set a higher value on closet prayer than ever, and that you#super[+] will make better and fuller use of closet prayer than you#super[+] have ever yet done. Consider what I say in my epistle to the reader, and labor to use this little treatise that I now put into your#super[+] hands in such a way that God may be glorified, that your#super[+] own souls may be edified, comforted, and encouraged in the ways of the Lord, and that you#super[+] may be my crown and joy in the great day of our Lord Jesus (1 Thess 2:19–20). So, wishing that “the favor of Him who dwelt in the burning bush” (Deut 33:16) may rest on you#super[+] and yours#super[+] forever, I take my leave and remain, dear friends, your#super[+] souls’ servant in our dear Lord Jesus,

